<http://data.silknow.org/object/ca078684-3a24-3b7d-ba9f-08f4e7fd88b3>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Woman's petticoat, front, 1750-1770, British; white silk satin, quilted with swags, tassels, zig-zag"@en , "Front of a woman’s petticoat of white silk satin, lined with white glazed worsted and wadded with a layer of wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with white silk thread in a narrow border of scrolls around the hem, underneath a horizontal pattern of swags with zig-zags, tassels, leaves and flowers.  The space above is filled with rows of curved lines. The front 3 panels of silk remain.  These were probably worn, apron-style, for fancy dress in the late 19th century, with an added waist band."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/78948bcb-860c-362a-b113-883d3da3af88> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Woman's petticoat, front, 1750-1770, British; white silk satin, quilted with swags, tassels, zig-zag"@en , "Front of a woman’s petticoat of white silk satin, lined with white glazed worsted and wadded with a layer of wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with white silk thread in a narrow border of scrolls around the hem, underneath a horizontal pattern of swags with zig-zags, tassels, leaves and flowers.  The space above is filled with rows of curved lines. The front 3 panels of silk remain.  These were probably worn, apron-style, for fancy dress in the late 19th century, with an added waist band."@en ;
